        "original_id": "85512dda-5e55-5b95-86f7-c6e395c3209c",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Organizations: Public Television 19, Inc.; Avila University\n- Stations: KCPT; KTBG; KCTV\n- Programs: Check, Please!\n- Places: Kansas City, Missouri; Kansas City, Kansas; Union Hill; Blue Valley; East 31st Street; 23rd Street and Stark Avenue\n- Roles: CBS affiliate; adult album alternative radio station; football coach\n\nFacts:\n- In 1999, Tim Johnson was hired by Avila University in Kansas City, Missouri, to start the school's football program.\n- In 2009, Check, Please! began airing in Kansas City on KCPT.\n- KCPT is owned by Public Television 19, Inc.\n- KCPT maintains studio facilities on East 31st Street in Kansas City, Missouri's Union Hill section.\n- KCPT shares its studio facilities with sister station KTBG, an adult album alternative radio station at 90.9 FM.\n- KCPT's studios are adjacent to the transmitter tower of KCTV.\n- KCPT's transmitter is located near 23rd Street and Stark Avenue in Kansas City, Missouri's Blue Valley section.\n- KCTV is virtual channel 5 and UHF digital channel 24.\n- KCTV is a CBS-affiliated television station licensed to Kansas City, Missouri, and it also serves Kansas City, Kansas.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
